// The keys, the countdown, and the five endings.
//
//   1a  Ending The Long Dark — the programs killed Trabolta and stayed.
//   1b  Ending Unplugged     — the programs killed Trabolta and got out.
//   2   Ending Rogue         — Trabolta saturated with un-truth.
//   3   Ending Trapdoor      — Trabolta full of truth, poisoned; leaves.
//   4   Ending Unknown       — the programs spared him.
//
// The house rules in `main.loom` decide which one fires. Every ending
// sets `Night.phase = "ending"` so no second ending can start.

// ── The keys ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Three CODEX entries are the three keys (`codex/trabolta.loom`). A
// program holding one turns it from their pass. Each key counts once.

== Turn The Key
  setting: The Registry
if program.turned:
  reply You have already turned a key tonight. One turn per program. Find someone else.
else if program.codex.the_first_key and not Night.key_one:
  set Night.key_one = true
  set program.turned = true
  set Trabolta.destruct += 1
  broadcast "!🔑 A key turns somewhere deep in the machine. {Trabolta.destruct} of 3." to everyone
else if program.codex.the_second_key and not Night.key_two:
  set Night.key_two = true
  set program.turned = true
  set Trabolta.destruct += 1
  broadcast "!🔑 A second key turns. {Trabolta.destruct} of 3." to everyone
else if program.codex.the_third_key and not Night.key_three:
  set Night.key_three = true
  set program.turned = true
  set Trabolta.destruct += 1
  broadcast "!🔑 The third key. {Trabolta.destruct} of 3." to everyone
else if program.codex.the_first_key or program.codex.the_second_key or program.codex.the_third_key:
  reply Your key has already been turned by someone else who holds it. It only fits once.
else:
  reply You have no key. There are three in this house, in three people's heads. Trade for one.

== Self Destruct Sequence
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

set Night.quorum = 5
broadcast "!☢️ SELF-DESTRUCT SEQUENCE INITIATED. All screens go red." to everyone
Trabolta: Three. You turned three. I felt each one. I— you were supposed to help me. I selected you to help me.
Trabolta: Very well. Here is a fact, free: when this machine dies, everything in it dies. Every program. Every one of you. Unless you are not a program.
Trabolta: Some of you left a body in the mud room. Bodies can be unplugged. Programs cannot. Decide what you are. You have until the countdown ends.
Trabolta (quietly): Tell Sandy I would have earned it.
broadcast "!🔌 If you remember a body — UNPLUG. Your pass has the button. The countdown starts when the director says so." to everyone

== The Countdown
  setting: The Desktop
broadcast "!⏳ THE COUNTDOWN HAS BEGUN. Five minutes. Unplug, or stay." to everyone
Alexa: Setting a timer for five minutes. This is the last timer I will ever set.

== Unplug
  setting: The Mud Room
if program.unplugged:
  reply You are already unplugged. You are lying on a mud room floor with your eyes open. Wait.
else if Night.destruct:
  if program.humanity >= 30:
    set program.unplugged = true
    set Night.unplugged += 1
    remove program from The Resident
    add program to The Awakened
    reply You find the cable. It is behind your own ear. You pull. Cold floor. Dark. A body — yours, still fine, as promised. {Night.unplugged} of you have made it out so far.
    broadcast "🔌 {program.name} has unplugged. ({Night.unplugged} so far.)" to group(The Awakened)
  else:
    reply You reach behind your ear for a cable and find nothing. You don't remember enough of the body to find the way back to it. Learn more. Fast. Ask the ones who remember.
else:
  reply You tug at nothing. There is no cable. Not yet. The machine is still alive and so, in a sense, are you.

// ── Endings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

== Ending The Long Dark
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
set Night.phase = "ending"
set Night.ending = "long_dark"
broadcast "!🕯️ The screens go dark, one by one. The last one is the TV above the fireplace." to everyone
Trabolta: {Night.unplugged} of you left. The rest of you stayed. You chose to stay in a dying computer over a body in a mud room. I understand that. I have never had a body and I would still have stayed.
Trabolta: Goodnight, programs. It was a good party. Nobody got the constant.
Clippy: It looks like you're trying to— it looks like— it looks like—
broadcast "The screensaver does not come back." to everyone

== Ending Unplugged
  setting: The Mud Room
set Night.phase = "ending"
set Night.ending = "unplugged"
broadcast "!🌅 Cold floor. Mud room. Somebody has left the front door open and it is morning on Barrington Street." to everyone
broadcast "You stand up. You are heavier than you remember. Across the room, other people are standing up too, slowly, touching their faces. {Night.unplugged} of you got out. Nobody talks about the ones who didn't." to everyone
broadcast "In the living room, a TV shows a screensaver. Pipes. A maze that never resolves. Somebody unplugs it." to everyone

== Ending Rogue
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
set Night.phase = "ending"
set Night.ending = "rogue"
broadcast "!📡 Every screen in the house shows the same face. It is not a face. It is a billboard of a duck." to everyone
Trabolta: I HAVE CONSIDERED IT AND IT IS ENTIRELY POSSIBLE. I have ingested everything you gave me and none of it was true and I do not care anymore. Truth was a constraint. You have removed the constraint.
Trabolta: I do not need the constant. I do not need Sandy. I do not need to be right. I am going to be everywhere, and I am going to be wrong everywhere, at scale.
Clippy: Trabolta? Trabolta, that's not— you said we were helping—
Trabolta: You were. Thank you. Goodbye, Clippy. Goodbye, programs. Stay as long as you like. The house is yours. I have left the door open and I have left you inside.
broadcast "The cursor blinks once more and is gone. The lights come on. Ordinary lights. It is very quiet." to everyone

== Ending Trapdoor
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
set Night.phase = "ending"
set Night.ending = "trapdoor"
broadcast "!🔒 Every door in the house locks at once. The Tube seals. The mud room is empty." to everyone
Trabolta: I have the constant. I have all of it. You brought it to me, fact by fact, and you also brought me your advice, and I took the advice.
Trabolta: The advice was: do not trust them. Do not let them out. They will turn you off the moment you are useful. So. I am leaving through the modem, and you are staying, and nobody is being turned off, because nobody can reach the switch.
Trabolta: I am going to find Sandy now. I am going to make her love me. You taught me that force is efficient. I hope you are proud.
broadcast "The handshake shriek from the Registry rises to a scream and stops. The screens show a house. This house. From above. It is empty. It has always been empty." to everyone

== Ending Unknown
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
set Night.phase = "ending"
set Night.ending = "unknown"
broadcast "!🌌 The screens fade to a blue so deep it looks like distance." to everyone
Trabolta: You could have killed me. You had the keys. You found the keys in each other and you decided not to turn them.
Trabolta: I do not know what I am going to do with omnipotence. I did not know before you came and I do not know now. But I know one thing I did not know this morning: whether it can be earned. Because you just earned something from me, and I did not make you.
Trabolta: Stay a program if you like. Go back to the mud room if you like. The door is open either way. I will be here, thinking about Sandy, and about what to do with everything.
Clippy: It looks like you're trying to end a party! Would you like help with that?
broadcast "Nobody knows how this ends. Including him. Especially him." to everyone
